{
  "name": "SHELL_QUAD",
  "formula": "=LAMBDA(nodes,values,point,LET(m,{ref}Shell.Rows3(nodes),v,{ref}Shell.AsColumn(values),p,{ref}Shell.Row3(point),valid,{ref}Shell.IsQuadValid(m),warp,IF(valid,{ref}Shell.IsQuadWarped(m),NA()),planeOk,IF(valid=FALSE,FALSE,IF(ISNA(warp),FALSE,IF(warp,TRUE,{ref}Shell.IsPointOnPlane(p,{ref}Shell.Node(m,1),{ref}Shell.Node(m,2),{ref}Shell.Node(m,3))))),nat,IF(planeOk,{ref}Shell.QuadNatural(m,p),NA()),xi,IF(AND(planeOk,ISNUMBER(INDEX(nat,1,1))),INDEX(nat,1,1),NA()),eta,IF(AND(planeOk,ISNUMBER(INDEX(nat,1,2))),INDEX(nat,1,2),NA()),wTry,IF(AND(ISNUMBER(xi),ISNUMBER(eta)),{ref}Shell.QuadN(xi,eta),NA()),inside,IF(ISNUMBER(INDEX(wTry,1,1)),{ref}Shell.WeightsInside(wTry),FALSE),resid,IF(inside,{ref}Shell.QuadResidual(m,p,xi,eta),NA()),onSurf,IF(inside,AND(ISNUMBER(resid),resid<={ref}Shell.SurfTol(m)),FALSE),IF(AND(onSurf,ROWS(m)=4,ROWS(v)=4),{ref}Shell.QuadValue(v,{ref}Shell.Clamp11(xi),{ref}Shell.Clamp11(eta)),NA())))",
  "comment": "Returns the scalar at a point on a 4-node shell quad. Arguments: nodes, values, point. nodes is 4 rows of x, y, z, counterclockwise. values is one number per node. point is x, y, z. A planar quad must lie on the plane of the first three nodes. A warped quad uses the bilinear surface. Natural coordinates outside -1 to 1, a point off the surface, or a collapsed quad returns #N/A. The surface tolerance is 1E-6 times the longest edge. Last Update at 2026-11-04.",
